Fix for clingox UPSTREAM-ISSUES U14: clasp asks Emscripten's getrusage for CPU
time, which is only a stub there.

Emscripten implements __syscall_getrusage as a stub that fills in the same
made-up times on every call (1.000002 s user, 3.000004 s system) and, in its
debug libc, prints "warning: unsupported syscall: __syscall_getrusage" each
time; a test run of clingox printed it 45,325 times. CPU times are differences
of two readings, so they are 0 either way. One reading is used whole: when a
thread of a parallel search ends (parallel_solve.cpp, threaded builds only),
where the made-up 4 s would be added. rusageTime now returns 0 under
Emscripten without calling getrusage. Against clingo v5.8.2; upstream's own
change for Emscripten (clasp#115) is not in 5.8.2.

diff --git a/clasp/src/timer.cpp b/clasp/src/timer.cpp
--- a/clasp/src/timer.cpp
+++ b/clasp/src/timer.cpp
@@ -79,10 +79,17 @@
 		: 0.0;
 }
 inline double rusageTime(int who) {
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+	// Emscripten only stubs getrusage: it returns the same made-up times on
+	// every call and its debug libc prints a warning each time.
+	(void)who;
+	return 0.0;
+#else
 	struct rusage usage;
 	getrusage(who, &usage);
 	return(static_cast<double>(usage.ru_utime.tv_sec) + static_cast<double>(usage.ru_utime.tv_usec / 1000000.0))
 		+ (static_cast<double>(usage.ru_stime.tv_sec) + static_cast<double>(usage.ru_stime.tv_usec / 1000000.0));
+#endif
 }
 double ProcessTime::getTime() {
 	return rusageTime(RUSAGE_SELF);
